-- FORWARD declarations for the generator of the vacuum theta function
-- (the constant C of Parameters.c): the standard hermitian spaces over
-- E = K(ζ_{N₁}), their finite Weil representation and theta functional,
-- the vacuum values, and the relation IsJetConjugate (the p-adic places
-- of ℂ are in GRH.Adelic.CuspForms); with the real definitions they are combined by (the
-- automorphisms of ℂ, those fixing K = ℚ(√−d)).
-- Source: grh-compact/src/New/Curve/ConjugateGenerator.lean
-- (exists_isJetConjugate_generator), Lib/Weil (Space, IsStd, vacElem,
-- finVec, finitePart, θ, ϱ), Lib/Weil/Construction/ConjugateJetDefs.lean
-- (Space.IsJetConjugate), New/Curve/JetDivisibility.lean (jetScale,
-- placePerm).
-- Encoding. Each FORWARD declaration below names one source object and
-- has a placeholder body (∅, or the typing alone for a predicate). Layer 4
-- replaces each body under the same name, with the source's meaning; the
-- statements of layer 5 that mention it are final as they stand. The
-- objects of one standard space (spaceRank, spacePoints, vacValue,
-- weilForms, finitePart, thetaValue, weilAction, ideleAct) are real,
-- read from GRH.Weil.Construction2 for V a ThetaSpace; stdSpaces and
-- finiteIdeles are defined in GRH.Proof.Data.Different.
-- Part of the GRH blueprint (layer 5, the argument).
